HST Office: a media error on Windows no longer opens a modal "Error" box that stops the slide show.

The Windows media player (MFPlay) showed every failure event as a raw English MessageBox owned by the slide
show window, for example "Activate failed to create mediasink ... (hr=0xC00D36FA)" when the PC has no audio
output device (a projector PC with HDMI audio unplugged, a test PC without speakers). The box took the focus,
keys no longer reached the show, and closing the show afterwards could take the document window with it. The
error is now only logged (SAL_WARN avmedia.win); the media object does not play, as in the reference
presentation app. Windows-only code: verified in a real slide show on a Windows test PC without audio device.

--- a/avmedia/source/win/player.cxx
+++ b/avmedia/source/win/player.cxx
@@ -347,15 +347,11 @@ void Player::ShowErrorMessage(HRESULT hrErr, bool bPopUpWin)
     HRESULT hr = StringCbPrintf(pszDest, sizeof(pszDest), pszFormat, msg.c_str(), hrErr);
     if (SUCCEEDED(hr))
     {
-        if (bPopUpWin)
-        {
-            MessageBox(mnFrameWnd, pszDest, TEXT("Error"), MB_ICONERROR);
-        }
-        else
-        {
-            SAL_WARN("avmedia.win",
-                     "Player::isPlaying failed with error code: " << std::string(pszDest));
-        }
+        // Never a modal message box: in a slide show it took the focus and stopped the show, e.g. on a PC
+        // without an audio output device (MF_E_NO_AUDIO_PLAYBACK_DEVICE, 0xC00D36FA). The media object just
+        // does not play, as in the reference presentation app.
+        SAL_WARN("avmedia.win", (bPopUpWin ? "media player error: " : "Player::isPlaying failed with error code: ")
+                                    << std::string(pszDest));
     }
 }
 
